3. Trial Period and prospective transition to paid licensing

The Trial Period begins when you first use a copy supplied under this license.
There is currently no fixed end date and no published commitment to a future
price or charging date. The Licensor reserves the right to end the zero-fee
trial for specified SDK versions or uses and offer continued use under a
separate written license, which may require an authorization fee.

To end the trial, the Licensor must publish a dated transition notice in the
official project or package documentation or release channel through which
the SDK is distributed. That notice must identify the affected versions or
uses, the date the trial ends, and how to obtain continued-use authorization.
The trial end date must be at least 30 calendar days after publication. Where
you have supplied a contact address for licensing notices, the Licensor will
also send the notice there. You should monitor the official licensing notices
while relying on this trial grant.

Until the notified end date, the existing trial remains free within its scope.
After that date, continued affected use or distribution requires a separate
applicable authorization; otherwise you must stop that affected use and
distribution. You are not required to purchase a license, and a notice does
not automatically create a payment obligation. No fee is charged retroactively
for use lawfully made during the Trial Period. A price announcement without
the notice and transition period required here does not end this trial.

